`),sampleAnswer:["Butan-2-ol is $\\mathrm{C_4H_{10}O}$. An isomer must have the same molecular formula, and a primary alcohol has its OH group on a carbon bonded to only one other carbon.","","One answer is butan-1-ol, $\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2CH_2CH_2OH}$:",jt("CCCCO",220,160),"The other correct answer is 2-methylpropan-1-ol, $\\mathrm{(CH_3)_2CHCH_2OH}$.","","A structure with the OH on the second carbon of the chain is still a secondary alcohol, and 2-methylpropan-2-ol is tertiary, so neither answers the question. Ethers such as ethoxyethane are isomers but are not alcohols."].join(`
