`),sampleAnswer:["The low magnitude means that much of the heat released by the burning propan-1-ol never reached the water, so $q$, and therefore $\\Delta_c H$, was underestimated. Any sound modification must reduce this loss. For example:","","- **Surround the burner and can with a draught shield** (e.g. a metal or cardboard screen) and put a lid on the can. This stops moving air carrying hot gases away from the can and reduces heat lost from the water surface, so more of the heat released is absorbed by the water.","","Other acceptable answers include insulating the sides of the can, lowering the can so the flame tip just touches its base, or improving the air supply so the fuel burns completely (a sooty yellow flame shows incomplete combustion, which releases less energy per mole)."].join(`
