`),marks:6},{question:"Stage 2 removed the dissolved carbon dioxide from the cider. Explain what effect skipping Stage 2 would have had on the calculated malic acid concentration.",sampleAnswer:["Dissolved carbon dioxide is acidic, because it reacts with water to form carbonic acid:","","$$\\mathrm{CO_2(aq) + H_2O(l) \\rightleftharpoons H_2CO_3(aq)}$$","","During the titration the sodium hydroxide would neutralise this carbonic acid as well as the malic acid, for example $\\mathrm{H_2CO_3 + 2NaOH \\rightarrow Na_2CO_3 + 2H_2O}$.","","The titre would therefore be larger than the volume needed for the malic acid alone. Because the calculation assumes all of the $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ reacted with malic acid, the calculated malic acid concentration would be **too high**."].join(`
