`),choices:a,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:['The words "first ideas" tell you this is the concept stage. The communication',"method should be quick to produce, easy for non-experts to understand and cheap","to change after feedback.","","Rendered concept sketches meet all three needs. Colour, shading and texture help","council members picture grass, water, paths and play equipment, and new sketches","can be made quickly if the council asks for changes.","","Why the others do not suit this stage:","- A full-size working prototype of a park is impossible and far too costly for","  ideas that may still change.","- A written specification lists requirements in words; it does not show layout","  or appearance.","- Dimensioned working drawings are for construction, after the concept has been","  approved, and are hard for non-specialists to read."].join(`
