`),sampleAnswer:["**Factor 1 — Back EMF of the motor:**","","As the motor speeds up, it generates a back EMF proportional to its","rotational speed $\\omega$:","$$\\mathcal{E}_{\\text{back}} = k\\omega$$","","The current drawn decreases:","$$I = \\frac{V - \\mathcal{E}_{\\text{back}}}{R}$$","","As speed increases, $I$ decreases, which reduces the motor's torque","($\\tau = kI$) and therefore the pulling force.","","**Factor 2 — Driving force decreases with speed:**","","The driving force at speed $v$ is:","$$F_{\\text{drive}} = \\frac{P_{\\text{mech}}}{v}$$","","For a fixed mechanical power output, the force decreases as speed increases.","","**Factor 3 — Friction (resistive force):**","","A constant friction force $F_f = \\mu mg$ opposes motion. At low speeds the","driving force exceeds friction and the mass accelerates. As speed increases,","the driving force falls until it equals the friction force.","","**Terminal (maximum) speed:**","","Maximum speed is reached when $F_{\\text{drive}} = F_f$:","$$\\frac{P}{v_{\\max}} = \\mu mg \\implies v_{\\max} = \\frac{P}{\\mu mg}$$","","Beyond this speed, friction exceeds the driving force, and the mass","decelerates. Hence the terminal speed is set by the motor's mechanical","power output and the frictional resistance."].join(`
