`),sampleAnswer:["**Mass defect for Step Y:**","","$$\\Delta m = m(^{13}\\text{C}) + m(^{1}\\text{H}) - m(^{14}\\text{N})$$","","$$\\Delta m = 13.003 + 1.007 - 14.003 = 0.007 \\ \\text{u}$$","","**Energy released:**","","$$E = \\Delta m \\times 931.5 = 0.007 \\times 931.5 \\approx 6.5 \\ \\text{MeV}$$","","**Why it differs from Step X (1.20 MeV):**","","Each step of the CNO cycle involves different reactant and product nuclei,","so the mass defect $\\Delta m$ for each reaction is different.","Step Y has a **greater mass defect** (0.007 u) than Step X, meaning","more mass is converted to energy, so Step Y releases **more energy**","(~6.5 MeV vs 1.20 MeV)."].join(`
