`),sampleAnswer:["The claim is largely valid. Many of the key results of atomic and nuclear","physics came from one of the two methods it describes, as the experiments","below show. It overstates the case slightly, however, because some advances","came from light interacting with matter, and from theory.","","**1. Steering particles with fields**","","- *Thomson (1897).* Cathode rays were bent by electric and magnetic fields.","  Thomson adjusted crossed fields until the beam went straight ($v = E/B$),","  then used the magnetic deflection alone to find the charge-to-mass ratio.","  The ratio was the same for every cathode material and was about 1800 times","  that of a hydrogen ion. This showed that atoms contain a light, negatively","  charged particle, the electron, so the atom is not indivisible.","- *Millikan (1909).* Charged oil drops were balanced in a uniform electric","  field ($qE = mg$). Every charge was a whole-number multiple of","  $1.602 \\times 10^{-19}$ C, so electric charge is quantised. Combined","  with Thomson's result, this gave the mass of the electron.","- *Mass spectrometers and accelerators.* Deflecting ions in magnetic fields","  separates isotopes by mass. Accelerators use fields to give particles","  enough energy to probe the nucleus.","","**2. Firing particles at matter**","","- *Geiger–Marsden (1909–1911).* Alpha particles were fired at thin gold foil.","  Most passed straight through, but a few bounced back through large angles.","  Rutherford concluded that the positive charge and most of the mass are",'  concentrated in a tiny nucleus, which replaced the "plum pudding" model.',"- *Chadwick (1932).* Alpha particles striking beryllium produced a neutral","  radiation that knocked protons out of paraffin. Conservation of momentum","  and energy showed that it was a neutral particle with about the mass of","  a proton, the neutron. This explained why atomic mass is larger than","  atomic number.","- *High-energy scattering.* Electrons scattered off protons at high energy","  showed that the proton has internal point-like parts (quarks). Collider","  experiments have confirmed many predictions of the Standard Model.","","**3. Limits of the claim**","","- Energy levels in atoms were revealed mainly by **light** interacting with","  matter: line spectra, and the photoelectric effect, which showed that light","  is quantised ($E = hf$). These are not particles steered by fields or","  fired at a target in the usual sense.","- Some ideas were theoretical first. Bohr's quantised orbits and de Broglie's","  matter waves were only later confirmed by experiment (for example, electron","  diffraction by Davisson and Germer, which is itself a scattering experiment).","","**Judgement**","","The claim is mostly correct. Deflection by fields revealed the electron and","the size of its charge, and scattering revealed the nucleus, the neutron and",'quarks. It is too strong to say "almost everything", though: spectroscopy,',"the photoelectric effect and theoretical models were also essential, and they","often guided which field and scattering experiments were carried out."].join(`
